    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "an audit log with action stop_send is saved, representing the status of the request to stop a server."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If that succeeded i.e. the request to stop a server is successfully sent, you can expect a log with action stop, representing the status of the stop operation i.e. the server stopped."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Note"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If you stop a server from inside, only a log entry with stop action will be added. This way, you can figure out if the server got stopped from the API or not:"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If there are 2 logs stop_send and stop, it is stopped via an API request"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If only stop is present ( no stop_send ), it means that the server is stopped by other means (stopped from inside, crashed, etc)."
    },
